# This binding's build products. cmetta.c and cmetta.h are the source; the shared
# library, the four examples, the C suite, the parity driver and the benchmark
# driver are all built by the Makefile here and are one machine's binaries.
libcmetta.so
examples/hello
examples/ops
examples/stream
examples/lower
kit/driver
benchmarks/cases

# The install products and the configuration stamp that decides when the
# installed library has to be rebuilt.
libcmetta.so.*
cmetta.pc
.enginedir-stamp
build/

# The C suite's own binaries, and the library the fault-injection tests link.
# Every one has its source beside it under the same stem, so the rule ignores
# the extensionless build product and keeps anything carrying an extension.
# Written as a pattern rather than a list because the list went stale: it named
# tests/test_cmetta alone while the Makefile's TESTS grew to eleven, and the ten
# others sat untracked in git status where one git add would have committed a
# machine's binary.
tests/test_*
!tests/test_*.*
tests/*.so
